The legal texts are the Constitution of the State of Hawaii, as published by the Hawaii Legislative Reference Bureau (lrb.hawaii.gov). Statutes and constitutions are
not copyrightable subject matter (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, 2020); only the law text is taken, never annotations, notes
or editorial material. The Bureau's site footer reserves rights in its own pages; the constitutional text is law.
Source: the Hawaii Legislative Reference Bureau, lrb.hawaii.gov.

